                "retweet_count": 2,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "MYTH: NPR/PBS provide unbiased, quality news coverage.\n\nFACT: While the broadcasters are statutorily required to ensure \u201cstrict adherence to objectivity and balance in all programs or series of programs of a controversial nature\u201d (47 U.S.C. \u00a7 396(g)(1)(D)), they have never complied with that legal obligation. Instead, they have flouted the law, going out of their way to produce news media that is favorable to left-leaning politicians and institutions. For this reason alone, NPR and PBS should be deprived of federal funding.\n\nAccording to an MRC report, recent examples include:\nPBS:\n1. 162 references to \u201cfar right\u201d vs only 6 references to \u201cfar left\u201d\n2. 6 times as many liberal political guests as conservative guests\n3. 88% positive coverage of the DNC vs 72% negative coverage of the RNC\n\nNPR:\n1. Banned coverage of the Hunter Biden laptop story, claiming it was a \u201cmere distraction\u201d\n2. Bans diversity of thought on climate-change issues\n3. Consistently cites Hamas propaganda and demonizes Israel",
